Offer RGB formats when EGL reports none for dma-buf import

The video appsink only accepts formats listed by
eglQueryDmaBufFormatsEXT, which flutter-pi only calls when EGL has
EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import_modifiers. Without that extension (virgl in
QEMU, among others) the list is empty, the appsink caps are EMPTY, no
decoder pad can link, and playback hangs forever.

Plain EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import is still required and still used, and
software-decoded frames are copied into a single-plane LINEAR GBM buffer
anyway, so offer the four 8-bit RGB formats in that case. A videoconvert
upstream of the appsink produces them. When EGL does report formats,
nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/src/plugins/gstreamer_video_player/frame.c
+++ b/src/plugins/gstreamer_video_player/frame.c
@@ -285,6 +285,25 @@
         formats = NULL;
     }

+    if (n_formats == 0) {
+        // Mira: without EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import_modifiers (virgl, among
+        // others) EGL reports no formats, the appsink caps end up empty, and no
+        // video can ever link. Plain EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import still works
+        // for single-plane RGB in a LINEAR GBM buffer, which is exactly what
+        // software-decoded frames are copied into - so offer those.
+        static const uint32_t fallback[] = { DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888, DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888, DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888 };
+        formats = malloc(ARRAY_SIZE(fallback) * sizeof *formats);
+        if (formats != NULL) {
+            for (size_t i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(fallback); i++) {
+                formats[i].format = fallback[i];
+                formats[i].modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
+                formats[i].external_only = false;
+            }
+            n_formats = ARRAY_SIZE(fallback);
+            fprintf(stderr, "[gstreamer video player] EGL reported no importable formats; using %d RGB fallback formats\n", n_formats);
+        }
+    }
+
     interface->gbm_device = gbm_device;
     interface->display = display;
     pthread_mutex_init(&interface->context_lock, NULL);
